ack  together with dummy lee jones he went on  the hunt for aliens as agent jay  yet in the first part released in 1997  he was not intended for this role at  all director barry sunfield actually  planned to cast david schwimmer who was  already known for his famous tv series  friends  schwimmer though had to turn down the  role because he was already directing  the movie  since you've been gone in which he also  played the lead and so the ambitious  young will smith became agent j do you  think the character would have gotten  the same hive with schwimmer in the role  robert downey jr had his big  breakthrough with iron man and was  finally able to put his past behind him  which had been plagued by drug scandals  as well as  other incidents he grew to become a  world star and is now a friend and  mentor to young acting colleagues like  tom holland  not only on screen but things could have  turned out very differently for him  the role of this steely superhero was  also offered to other actors  including tom cruise when he was asked  about this in a later interview he  responded that he loved robert downey jr  and couldn't imagine  anyone else in the role an appraisal  that proves greatness and is certainly  shared by  many including us the lord of the rings  has shaped many acting careers  for instance actor elijah wood is always  associated with frodo  wiggle mortensen with aragorn and sean  astin with the character of samwise  gumji  it is different regarding the role of  gandalf since actor ian mckellen had  already been a hollywood star for  years however it is controversial that  it was actually not mcallen but james  bond star sean connery who was intended  for the role of the great wizard  the rumors even go so far as to claim  that the producers were so eager to hire  connery that they promised him 15  of the revenues plus 10 million us  dollars for each movie  if he were to sign the contract in an  interview however connery said that he  didn't understand 